            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 7:38 p.m. Central Daylight Time Friday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for Southeastern Manitoba. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Pointe du Bois, Falcon Lake, West Hawk Lake, Shoal Lake Reserve, Ste. Rita, Hadashville and Rennie. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
